From 87d4888d67d65ca3f1df5eff4b57cc64cd1544b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:24:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 195/217] fix: SVOGI disappeared because a comment line lost
 its // and ended the .cfx parse

c334c969 rewrote the three RT_* #define comments into a block above the defines. One
line of that block was written with a literal newline inside it, so CommonSVO_RT.cfi
line 310 is

    ') -> NULL -> the engine

with no // in front of it: live text at file scope. CParserBin::GetNextToken hands the
apostrophe (eT_sing_quote) to CParserBin::ParseObject, which walks the FX command list,
misses, warns

    FXBin parser found token ''' which was not one of the list (Skipping).

(ParserBin.cpp:2495-2519) and returns eTS_invalid. "Skipping" is a lie: eTS_invalid ends
the while (Parser.ParseObject(sCommands)) loop in ShaderFXParseBin.cpp:3848, so every
object below that point - all 13 techniques of Total_Illumination.cfx - never exists.
No shader is compiled, so there is no compile error either; SVOGI simply does nothing.

Fix is the comment, nothing else. No token of the shader code changes, so the stage 2D
packing round trip is byte-identical.

Verified by re-implementing SaveBinShader + PreprocessTokens(0) + GetNextToken/ParseObject
in python and running it over the three revisions of the four SVO shader files:

    c0857963  154 file-scope objects, 13 techniques   (known good)
    e3695d03  154 file-scope objects, 13 techniques   (specular packing - clean)
    c334c969   81 file-scope objects,  0 techniques   stops at token 6416, eT_sing_quote
    HEAD      154 file-scope objects, 13 techniques

e3695d03's new constructs were audited against the same tokenizer and all survive it:
ConvertToAscii reproduces `hueCode % 6`, `code&255u`, `code/=256u`, `1e-5f`, `(float3)1.f`
and `(uint3)clamp((int3)(...))` as valid HLSL, and `#define RT_HUE_RANGE 6` expands inside
`(RT_HUE_RANGE - 1)` to `(6-1)`.

Also adds scene-notes/rt/tools/cryfx_lint.py (outside git) as a pre-deploy check for this
whole class of silent failure; it reproduces both the R1 crash of e3695d03 and the R2
technique loss of c334c969, and is clean on 123 of the 124 stock CryFX files.

Revalidated with scene-notes/rt/tools/rtharness2: ShadePS, ConeTracePS, DemosaicPS and
UpScalePS in four flag sets plus BuildRayTracingLightListCS - 13 compiles, 0 errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
index a1dd7094..e31a17b9 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
@@ -305,10 +305,12 @@ float PackRGB(const float3 col)
 // the round trip is deterministic and testable.
 ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 
-// CryFX pitfall: never put a // comment on a #define line. SaveBinShader copies the macro body
-// without its newline and SkipComments then does strchr(buf, '
-') -> NULL -> the engine
-// dereferences it at startup (2026-09-14 crash). Comments go on their own lines.
+// CryFX pitfall (2026-09-14): never put a // comment on a #define line. SaveBinShader copies the
+// macro body up to but not including its newline, and SkipComments then searches that buffer for
+// a newline, finds none, and the caller dereferences the null result at startup. And every line
+// of a comment block needs its own // - a line without one is live file-scope text, and the very
+// first token of it that is not an FX command makes CParserBin::ParseObject return eTS_invalid,
+// which ends the ParseBinFX loop and silently drops every technique below it.
 // RT_HUE_RANGE: levels per channel in the reflectance hue code (6^3 = 216).
 // RT_SMOOTH_STEPS: smoothIdx in [0, 255]. RT_GREY_STEPS: greyIdx in [0, 255].
 #define RT_HUE_RANGE     6
